# Wedding Gift Registry — Project Memory

Couple: **Sagar & Krithika**. Repo docs: `docs/implementation-plan.md`, `docs/phase-1-database-setup.md`.

## Stack (do not deviate)

Next.js App Router · TypeScript · Tailwind · Supabase Postgres/Auth/Storage · Vercel.  
**No** Spring/Java, separate backend, Docker, Redis, Kafka, GraphQL, Redux, Prisma/Drizzle, service role in Next.js.

## Locked decisions

- Public registry: `/registry`. `/` = future landing only.
- No `/gifts/[id]`. No pricing anywhere. No guest notes/emails.
- Images: **Supabase Storage required** (`gift-images`). Not external URLs as primary.
- Categories (DB): Kitchen, Home, Decor, Experiences, **Gift Cards last**. UI has **All**.
- Normal gifts: one reservation. Gift Cards: one gift, `is_unlimited=true`, unlimited reserves.
- Public shows only **“Reserved”** — never guest names or counts.
- Guests reserve with **name only** via `reserve_gift` RPC. No guest cancel.
- Admin: Supabase Auth + `public.admins` allowlist. JWT + RLS for CRUD/uploads.
- Guest reserve UX success: `Thank you, <name> ❤️` / `This gift has been reserved.`
- Public UI must match the approved Style One mockup: cream parchment, maroon titles, gold ornaments, forest-green rounded category bar with gold corner filigree + icon nav, centered invitation copy flanked by Tamil Nadu (left) and Kerala (right) sepia sketches with region labels, gift grid after the category bar, four blessings columns above the footer. English only. No couple photo / garland side columns in the approved composition.

## Implementation order (current)

1. Done: scaffold, DB, public registry (Phase 0–2)
2. Done: Admin auth + gift CRUD/images (Phase 4–5)
3. Done: Guest reserve dialog (Phase 3)
4. Done: Visual polish + deploy docs (Phase 6)
5. Optional later: full landing page, CAPTCHA, OG images (Phase 7)

## Agent rules

- Prefer Server Components + Server Actions; Client only for forms/tabs/dialogs.
- Keep dependencies minimal (`@supabase/ssr`, `@supabase/supabase-js`, `zod`).
- Never add `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` to the app.
- Before changing schema/product rules, re-read `docs/implementation-plan.md`.
